          "kicker": "Union restructure",
          "heading": "WRU explores two Welsh clubs in Gallagher Prem despite cutting to three",
          "body": "The WRU has told the Professional Rugby Board it is exploring the possibility of two Welsh clubs playing in the Gallagher Prem, a development that complicates a plan already under fire. Directors voted unanimously to cut the four professional teams to three, with one licence each in the east, centre and west, and Ospreys and Scarlets competing for the western slot unless they merge. A summit with the four clubs is expected in December, and the union is due to confirm the three licensed teams by next March."
        },
